  "id": "cranial-index",
  "term": "cranial index",
  "definition": "In this historical source, cranial index means a numerical skull value derived from head measurements and used to compare overall head size across groups such as men and women, ages, and diagnoses. It is treated as an indicator of the size of the head rather than as a description of head shape.",
